        "topic": "PREVIOUS ASSESSMENT",
        "text": "Mason Kessler underwent a Multidisciplinary Psycho-educational Evaluation in fourth grade at NCSA. Score summaries are located in Addendum 2 at the end of this report. This assessment indicated Mason Kessler had above average cognitive ability with no areas of processing weakness, including auditory, visual, sensory motor, verbal, attention and reasoning. While sensory motor processing fell within the average range, a poor pencil grip was noted to impact speed of writing. Observations of executive functioning identified a broad level of concerns, but Mason Kessler was accessing his education and making growth. He demonstrated average to well above average academic skills. Mason Kessler had friends and his non-verbal as well as pragmatic language skills fell within the average range. A 504 Plan was developed as educational need could not be identified.",
        "source": "approved-anonymized case 006 (signed section excerpt)"
      }
    ]
  }
}

